      ],
      "solution": "For a, literal IV row/main-column addresses (4.3,0),(6.2,0),(8.9,0),(10,0),(50,0),(75,0) give roots in order 2.074,2.490,2.983,3.162,7.071,8.660. For b, (1.2,5),(14,7),(20,8),(40,1),(83,2) give 1.118,3.834,4.561,6.332,9.121. For c: 1.143 uses row1.1/main4=1.068, correction3=1 ->1.069; 4.835 uses row4.8/main3=2.198, correction5=1 ->2.199; 60.37 uses row60/main3=7.765, correction7=4 ->7.769; 81.92 uses row81/main9=9.050, correction2=1 ->9.051. Each IV correction integer is multiplied by 0.001. For d under explicit four-significant-figure preprocessing: 1.0058 ->1.006, row1.0/main0=1.000 plus correction6=3 ->1.003; 6.83251 ->6.833, row6.8/main3=2.613 plus correction3=1 ->2.614; 20.156 ->20.16, row20/main1=4.483 plus correction6=7 ->4.490. Do not claim these preprocessing results are the unique unstated historical answers."
