      ],
      "solution": "a: sqrt6.52 approx2.553 from row6.5/main2. 652=6.52*10^2 ->25.53;6520=65.2*10^2 ->10*8.075=80.75;0.652=65.2*10^-2 ->0.8075. b: sqrt3.278 uses row3.2/main7=1.808 plus correction8=2 ->1.810;3278=32.78*10^2 uses row32/main7=5.718 plus correction8=7 ->5.725 then *10=57.25;0.03278=3.278*10^-2 ->0.1810;327800=32.78*10^4 ->572.5. Multiplying a radicand by100 multiplies its nonnegative root by10, not100. The normalization coefficients alternate between3.278 and32.78 when the decimal-shift parity changes."
