      ],
      "solution": "a:376.8=3.768*100. IV row3.7/main6=1.939 plus correction8=2 gives1.941, scaled root19.41. For37.68, row37/main6=6.132 plus correction8=7 gives6.139. Actual table sum19.41+6.139=25.549; selected final four-significant-figure result25.55. b:82340=8.234*10^4; row8.2/main3=2.869 plus correction4=1 ->2.870, scaled root287.0.8234=82.34*100; row82/main3=9.072 plus correction4=2 ->9.074, scaled root90.74. Actual table difference287.0-90.74=196.26; selected final four-significant-figure result196.3. The direct-root reference difference is about196.20808 but is not the table-route result. Carrying table-number digits in arithmetic does not make them exact input data."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "812",
      "source_task_count": 1,
      "task_ids": [
        "method-comparison"
      ],
      "solution": "For nonnegative2,3, sqrt2*sqrt3=sqrt6 exactly. Captured sqrt2 main value1.414 and sqrt75 main8.660 imply the supplemental table-derived sqrt3 approximation8.660/5=1.732 because75=25*3. Their product1.414*1.732=2.449048. A direct sqrt6 table lookup gives2.449. In the original two-direct-lookup comparison, simplifying first replaces two root lookups and a multiplication with one lookup; with this bounded supplied-cell route the separate-root route even requires an extra division. Thus method2 is more convenient. This convenience conclusion does not prove an unconditional error advantage. The intermediate table product and final table value are recorded, not just the plan."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "813",
      "source_task_count": 2,
      "task_ids": [
        "a",
        "b"
      ],
      "solution": "a:sqrt7*sqrt5=sqrt35; captured IV row35/main0=5.916; nearest0.01 ->5.92. b:sqrt3.1*sqrt4.5=sqrt13.95; row13/main9=3.728 plus correction5=7 thousandths ->3.735. Explicit positive half-up rounding of this table number to0.01 ->3.74. Direct exact-input sqrt13.95=3.734969879... would round to3.73, so this method-specific response must not claim unconditional accuracy to0.01 for the true root. Source request and selected table/final-rounding procedure are both retained. Corrected entries are not subject to the direct-main half-unit guarantee."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "814",
      "source_task_count": 4,
      "task_ids": [
        "root18",
        "root2",
        "approximate-product",
        "exact-product"
      ],
      "solution": "Literal main sqrt18 approx4.243 and sqrt2 approx1.414. Multiplication of obtained table numbers gives4.243*1.414=5.999602. A chosen four-significant-figure display is6.000, but the unrounded arithmetic product does not have seven reliable significant figures. Independently sqrt18*sqrt2=sqrt36=6 exactly, orsqrt18=3sqrt2 so the product is3*2=6. Keep numerical approximation and exact product logically distinct; neither rounded factor equals its exact irrational root."
    },
    {
      "source_number": "815",
